  "description": "SIKH EMPIRE: AR gobindshahi rupee (10.39g), Amritsar, VS1865, KM-A20.2, Herrli-01.20.04, lovely VF to EF, ex Butalia Collection. Gobindshahi rupees dated VS1862-1865 follow a lighter standard, typically 10.45g to 10.65g, usually even lighter for the last year VS1865 (10.3g to 10.5g). The Gobindshahi rupee was not resumed until VS1895, when the weight standard was restored to the Nanakshahi standard of about 11.14g.",
